# The modem's calls, the image built with COM2 the modem's line and the log
# on COM3: the buffers they refuse; then a modem's answer to ATI, which
# comes whole (30 bytes: ATI and CR echoed, the name, OK) also while the
# kernel is busy writing 1,920 bytes to the console and its log. The timer
# fetches what an interrupt left, if one was lost (on Bochs a UART's
# interrupt is lost when another UART on its line is touched).
program: devices
define: DEVICES_MODEM
modem: hayes
match: contains
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs dosbox-x
---
serial: read into the code: error 1
serial: read across the data's limit: error 1
serial: read through a null ES: error 1
serial: write from a null DS: error 1
serial: write too much: error 3
modem: idle: answer of 30 bytes
modem: while the log is written: answer of 30 bytes
modem: after: answer of 30 bytes
